WEBVTT

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.920
Thank you!

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.820
Hey, hey. Did Yoshida-cchi reply?

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.670
About me coming over after work!

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.660
Let me see.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.870
What does it say?

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.580
"Sure, but Asami's coming over too much."

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.140
Well, it's summer break! And we're soul mates!

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.160
Right?

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.890
Okay, I guess I'll go stock the shelves.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.110
There it is again.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.350
I see that car parked here a lot lately.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.020
They never come in to buy anything.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.320
It left.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.110
I wonder what their deal is.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.780
Maybe they're just bored?

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.830
Wow, not this type of problem again.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:31.960
What?

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.590
Look, look.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:39.450
"Yearning"

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:42.070
"Choose from the following the reason 
why Toyotaro said the underlined phrase (A)."

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.330
It looks normal to me.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.730
Yeah, but it annoys me.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:53.150
How's the guy who made this problem 
supposed to know what the character was thinking?

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.690
The author's probably saying, 
"No, that wasn't what I meant at all, dude."

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:01.840
I don't think he's saying 
those words specifically, but maybe.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:02.910
Right?

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.620
Man, forget this stuff.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:09.080
But I have to study for my exams.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.580
My promising future depends on them.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:21.590
Yoshida-san, living with you... 
I finally...

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:27.810
I-I can finally think about the future.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.310
The future?

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:35.340
I don't have to think about where
I'm running to. But where I'm going.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:36.900
Sayu...

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.580
So...

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.180
Will you be with me just a little longer?

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.580
<i>"My future," huh?</i>

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:57.860
<i>Going back home, to Hokkaido, 
where my parents are...</i>

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.770
<i>And then what?</i>

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.550
What's wrong?

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.310
You look like your soul fell 
out of your body.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.170
U-Uh, no...

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.060
I was thinking of what to have for dinner.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.660
Oh, like a housewife?

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.270
It's tough trying to come up 
with a meal every day.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:22.240
I know just the thing!

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:27.340
There's this boxed lunch we get a ton of 
at our store during exam season.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.450
Do you know it?

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.960
Sayu-chan again.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:50.670
I'm jealous. I don't even have his number.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.890
Yoshida-kun?

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.350
What?

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:59.610
I had a question about the documents 
you just sent over.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.320
Can you explain this part 
a little more in depth?

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.990
Okay.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.880
Try to have it ready 
for the afternoon meeting.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:11.840
Okay.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:13.000
Thanks!

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.510
Mishima-san?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:32.430
Gotou-san, would you like 
to eat lunch with me?

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.410
Huh?

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.060
Are those Chinese noodles any good?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.920
I don't know. I've never had them.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.780
You haven't, huh?

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:50.410
And?

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:53.370
You wanted to talk about something, right?

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:01.540
What do you think about Yoshida-senpai lately?

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:04.800
Yoshida-kun? How do you mean?

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:09.510
What is it?

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.720
You looked so serious.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:13.930
Did I?

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.240
You did.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.180
His appearance has been a lot neater.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.810
He's not so pale anymore, either.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.230
And he's leaving right at closing time.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:28.200
The rumors say he got a girlfriend.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.500
Um...

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.810
You know, don't you, Gotou-san?

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:33.910
Know what?

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:39.620
That he has... well, not a girlfriend, but...

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.330
Sayu-chan, right?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.870
So you did know.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:46.680
Yeah.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.990
We've talked.

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:52.090
She's a nice girl.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:55.260
You're not worried?

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:59.560
She might take him.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.000
Sayu-chan would?

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.230
What is it?

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:08.610
No, if it happens, it happens.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:13.530
You can't control other people's feelings, 
no matter how much you want to.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:15.330
Still...

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:17.450
Even if I were to interfere somehow

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:21.370
and get the result I wanted 
in a way that wasn't natural,

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.000
how long would it last?

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:26.460
W-Well...

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.720
Does that mean there's no point in trying?

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:34.280
I won't say that.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.950
But if you try to force things 
to be something they shouldn't be,

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:40.890
when time passes, 
they'll just go back to how they were.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.610
What?

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:48.310
You're just scared.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:53.700
Because even if you work hard 
to get what you want, you may lose it someday.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:58.620
So you're just saying to wait 
for things to work out, right?

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.580
Mishima-san...

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:00.580
I...

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:06.840
I'm much more scared of losing the things 
I could've had because I didn't do anything!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:07.790
Mishima-san!

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:15.110
You're too loud.

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:17.430
I'm sorry.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:24.560
Well, until we know exactly 
how he feels about Sayu-chan,

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:28.230
isn't it better just to wait?

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.610
You're talking as if this doesn't involve you.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:33.320
It doesn't.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.780
But you love Yoshida-senpai, don't you?

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.060
I do.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:47.210
That's why I think anything I did 
wouldn't matter.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:52.170
What's wrong with this woman?

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.640
You're so cute, Mishima-san.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:00.390
And you're creepy, Gotou-san!

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.530
<b>Today's dinner is something special!</b>

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.380
Yoshida-senpai?

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.470
Mishima? What's up? Was there a problem?

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:22.940
Want to go see a movie?

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:23.860
Huh?

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:27.560
You don't have to look that annoyed.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:30.130
No, I didn't mean that.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.380
But she's making something special 
for dinner tonight.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.680
Okay, fine, I guess...

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:43.240
Give me your contact info instead.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.230
Why?

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:50.940
You've given it to Sayu-chan 
and Gotou-san, right?

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:53.130
I did, yeah...

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:57.450
So you should be able to give it to me, 
since we're co-workers.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.030
What?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:02.910
Let me see me your phone. 
I'll give you mine, too.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:08.620
Here.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.630
But you know...

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:16.870
Even if I do give you my contact info, 
what will you talk to me about?

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:22.050
I can understand wanting it 
from someone who talked a lot,

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:26.430
but I don't send messages to people 
I don't need to talk to.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:30.250
And even if you send me something, 
I can't send you a good answer.

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:34.140
Wait, what the heck?

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:36.740
So basically...

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:41.680
You're saying that you're
not attractive enough to be worth

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:45.000
giving your contact info 
to unless there's a special reason?

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.620
W-Well, something like that.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.920
Really...

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:58.890
It's not right to decide everything 
by your own standards.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.990
You pretend to care about others,

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:06.930
but in the end, you always put the way 
you see things over everything else!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.140
And then, even though you're only doing 
the things you want to,

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:13.600
you convince yourself 
you're doing it for their sake!

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.650
It's a bad habit of yours!

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:21.320
It may be good enough for you...

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:28.120
But how am I supposed to feel, 
after I already grabbed the phone from your hand?

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:31.750
How do you feel?

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:36.210
I'm telling you...

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:39.920
I'm in love with you, Yoshida-senpai!

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:47.770
A little, anyway.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.100
"A little," huh?

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:59.370
Anyway, I want your contact info.

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:02.570
So I forced you to give it to me.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.500
Is that good enough?

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:09.580
Well, if you say so, I guess it has to be.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.210
<b>Can I ask you to a movie again sometime?</b>

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:26.340
<b>Sure.</b>

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:32.490
You're like a little kid. 
You try to do what people tell you.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:39.370
I like that about you.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.770
So you meant katsudon?

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:58.970
You know how Asami's taking exams, right?

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:02.510
She told me that every year 
during exam season,

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:06.010
the convenience store 
stocks a bunch of katsudon.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.740
Around February?

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.640
Yes. To win <i>(katsu)</i> at your exams, supposedly.

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:13.640
That's a really old joke.

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:15.520
I see.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:18.610
I just heard it for the first time, 
so I laughed really hard.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.070
Let's eat.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:28.030
So, what am I supposed to be winning at?

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:33.450
I dunno. Winning over yourself?

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:37.240
They say you're your
own worst enemy, after all.

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:41.770
Yum!

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:45.520
<i>I'm my own worst enemy, huh?</i>

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:52.970
<i>I've made a lot of choices to help Sayu.</i>

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.120
<i>At least, I thought I had, but...</i>

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:02.660
<i>But I was just doing the things 
I wanted to do?</i>

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.980
Yoshida-san?

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.490
Is it not good?

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.980
No, it's good, but...

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:10.990
But?

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:15.500
It feels really weird to eat katsudon 
in the middle of summer?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.090
I know. It's really hot.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:18.940
Yeah.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:19.820
Right?

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:33.430
You seem more into it than usual.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:38.640
I've been busy with work and haven't managed 
to clean out all the little corners.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.260
I see.

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.360
I'll help, too.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.700
No, no. You can just relax.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.680
But the futon's heavy, right?

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.030
Yeah, but...

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:57.420
That's not the issue!

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:00.080
The chores are my job!

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.530
I can help a little, right?

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:05.400
It's my day off, and I'm bored.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:06.390
No!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.020
S-Sorry!

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:20.350
Sayu...

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.060
Um, what?

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.030
The rag.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:28.960
I-I'm sorry, really!

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.750
Take it off now, and I'll wash it!

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.360
Got it, got it.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.980
You should take a shower, too.

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:39.240
Your hair's a mess.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.040
Seriously?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.140
Seriously.

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:45.420
I see. Okay, I'll do that then.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:16:00.180
Yoshida-san, should I not touch 
what's in the box in the closet?

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:02.940
No, it's fine.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.830
Whew!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.900
<b>All this crap is yours, and it's taking up space.
If you don't need it, throw it out! -Mom</b>

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.790
<b>Graduation Album</b>

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.190
Yoshida-san in high school.

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:49.520
Oh, that.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.730
Your girlfriend?

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:54.700
I guess.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.740
You had a girlfriend, huh?

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:00.460
What, is that weird?

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:02.580
No, that's not it.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.540
But like...

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:09.380
You never talked about anything like that.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.110
She's pretty.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:14.160
She was.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.590
She was the senpai everybody admired.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.750
"Senpai"...

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:21.160
Gotou-san, your girlfriend...

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:24.240
You really like pretty older girls, huh?

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:25.290
Quiet.

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:28.640
Why are you blushing? I'm just teasing you.

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:31.690
Why do I have to be teased by a little kid?!

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:34.650
True. Sorry.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.990
I kind of remembered something.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:49.920
She told me I was clingy once.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.300
Clingy?

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:57.510
She said she didn't want somebody 
who cared about her so much.

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:02.860
You were that into her, Yoshida-san?

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:04.970
Well, we were dating.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:09.520
Isn't it natural to care about someone?

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:14.160
If you really love someone, 
you want them to be smiling all the time.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.940
To be happy.

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:20.470
You want to make them happy yourself
 if you can, right?

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:23.940
Because, well, you're giving 
the relationship your all, right?

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:30.880
Then...

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:34.090
What about me?

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:41.720
Y-Yoshida-san, no smoking!

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:44.550
Oh, right. The smell gets everywhere.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.450
I'm going on break.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:13.480
It's back.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:15.670
Look. The luxury car.

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:18.810
You're right.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:23.860
Huh? Is it stopping to buy something?

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:27.690
They've got a driver?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.480
What's wrong?

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.220
Do you know them?

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:46.910
Someone you don't want to see?

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.660
Stay down. Get into the office.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.010
Go.

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:15.820
Sorry to interrupt your work.

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:19.980
Here's my card.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.320
<b>CEO & President 
Ogiwara Kazuto</b>

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.230
Huh...

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:27.370
I'm looking for a girl named Ogiwara Sayu.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.040
Does she work here?

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:32.090
Never heard that name.

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.000
Sure you don't mean a different store?

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:36.110
Where's your manager?

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:37.800
Not in today.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.100
If you want to leave
a message, I can relay it.

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:45.740
I see.

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:48.930
Your brother?

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:51.930
Your brother's here?

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:54.060
He's here looking for you?

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:56.850
I think so.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.420
<i>My brother's here.</i>

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:07.450
<i>He's been looking for me.</i>

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:11.420
<i>But I'm still not ready 
to go back to that house.</i>

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:15.210
You can come out now.

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:19.420
Um, thank you for helping me.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.990
Nah, I just don't like guys like that.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.130
Like what?

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:32.810
People with power, who think they can use 
that power to control other people's lives?

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:36.910
But he's serious.

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:40.040
You might not be able to
keep running for much longer.

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:43.070
